      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To elucidate complications and unfavorable side effects of diagnostic exercise and dobutamine stress echocardiography."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL",
          "content": "Results of exercise (n=1969) and dobutamine (n=414, 34% with the use of atropine) stress echocardiography conducted in 2 centers for diagnosis of coronary heart disease. Mean age of patients 54,4+/-9,4 years."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There were no deaths or life threatening complications. Disturbances of cardiac rhythm and conduction (31% during exercise and 61% during dobutamine stress tests) were most frequent events. One of 13 exercise and of 5 dobutamine stress tests was stopped because of complications or side effects. Of 15 cases of ventricular tachycardia and 16 of hypotension (lowering of blood pressure by 20 mm Hg) 9 and 13, respectively, occurred during dobutamine tests. There were differences between centers in frequency of atropine use during dobutamine tests and therapy of stress induced chest pain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The data confirmed that both exercise and dobutamine/atropine stress echocardiography could be safely used in diagnosis of coronary heart disease."
        }
      ]},
